course: dictionary
lesson: 3633
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning is right. «The detective found fingerprints on the window.» Here fingerprints are the marks that fingertips leave on a surface, so you can tell the meaning from the detective and the window.
explain: Now read this: «Every gorilla has its own pattern of nose wrinkles, like a fingerprint.» The word is used to compare. It means a pattern that is special to one thing and not the same as any other. Try your meaning in the sentence: "every gorilla has its own pattern, like a special pattern" makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Fingerprint can also be a verb, a doing word. «The police fingerprinted the thief» means they took a record of his fingerprints. When you see a word that could be a noun or a verb, look at the words around it. Does it name a thing, or does it say what someone does?
fact: A fingerprint is the pattern of tiny lines on the tip of each finger.
fact: «Fingerprints are ridges that help us grip.»
fact: «Every person's fingerprints are different, even identical twins'.»
fact: As a verb, «fingerprint» means to take a record of someone's fingerprints, for example by the police.
fact: A fingerprint can also mean a special mark that shows who made something or where it came from.
exercise: «The detective found fingerprints on the window.» What are fingerprints here? | Small fish that swim in the sea | Loud noises made by a door | *Marks left by fingertips on a surface | Lines drawn on paper by a child
exercise: «Every gorilla has its own pattern, like a fingerprint.» What does pattern suggest? | A shape that is hard to see | *A special shape that is not the same as any other | A very common shape that everyone has | A sweet smell
exercise: «Fingerprints are ridges that help us grip.» What do the ridges help us do? | Sing | Swim | Sleep | *Grip
test: «The police fingerprinted the thief.» What does fingerprinted mean here? | Washed the window clean | Ran very fast away from the house | Hid behind a door | *Took a record of his fingerprints
test: Phones can unlock with a fingerprint scanner. What does the scanner do? | Measures how much it is raining | *Checks the pattern of your finger to unlock the phone | Cooks your food | Plays your favourite music
exam: In «Her cooking has a fingerprint all her own: the spice always gives it away», what does fingerprint mean? | *A special mark that shows who made something | A thin line of ink | A sharp pencil | A cold drink
